# Creature tier rows (Monsters.md)

## Rule

In **`## Creature families`**, each dungeon family has **exactly four tier rows**, in order: **Worker → Minion → Elite → Boss**. No fifth tier row (e.g. no separate “Backup boss” row).

**Asset / note cells may list anything:** multiple Fab candidates, Hi3D + Fab options, backup bosses, rejected picks, UE paths, pipeline detail — unrestricted.

**Intruders** stay in their own section; not part of the family tier grid.

## Table style

- **`## In UE`** — full tier grid (6 families × 4 tiers); `/Game/Monsters/` paths only; `—` = missing import.
- **`## Not in UE yet`** — pending Fab / Hi3D / CC picks **only for tiers not in the first table** (and alternates). Do **not** duplicate rows that are already in UE.
- Normal column widths; pipeline detail under **Art direction**.

## Do not

- Bloat rows with full CC/AccuRIG prose duplicated per creature unless the user asks.
- Overwrite the file from git without merging local edits.
- Overwrite reference image paths; version per `reference-images-versioning.mdc`.
